          },
          "charspan": [
            0,
            439
          ]
        }
      ],
      "text": "Crescent CLO 2026-2 (the 'Transaction') is a $525.0 million cash flow collateralized loan obligation managed by Crescent Capital Management, LLC. The Transaction is structured as a U.S. dollar-denominated investment vehicle primarily targeting senior secured corporate loans. The Issuer is Crescent CLO 2026-2, Ltd., an exempted company incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands, and Crescent CLO 2026-2, LLC acts as the Co-Issuer."
    },
    {
      "element_index": 5,
      "element_type": "TextItem",
      "label": "text",
      "self_ref": "#/texts/5",
      "hierarchy_level": 2,
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 1,
      "provenance": [
        {
          "page_no": 1,
          "bbox": {
            "l": 59.7599983215332,
            "t": 491.8399963378906,
            "r": 535.89990234375,
            "b": 431.55999755859375,
            "coord_origin": "CoordOrigin.BOTTOMLEFT"
          },
          "charspan": [
            0,
            350
          ]
        }
      ],
      "text": "The capital structure is designed with multiple tranches of rated debt, providing varied risk-return profiles for institutional investors. Subordinated notes represent the equity component, absorbing the first loss in the event of portfolio credit deterioration. The non-call period is two years, providing stability during the initial ramp-up phase."
    },
