      ],
      "summary": "**Purpose**  \nThis table presents the key terms and capital structure of Crescent CLO 2026‑2, Ltd.\n\n**Key Information**\n\n- **Issuer & Manager** – Crescent CLO 2026‑2, Ltd.; Collateral Manager: Crescent Capital Management.  \n- **Timing** – Closing Date: September 15 2026; Legal Final Maturity: October 20 2038; Reinvestment Period: 5 Years (2031).  \n- **Collateral & Capital** – Target Collateral: **$500,000,000**.  \n- **Senior Note Classes**  \n  - *Class A*: **$315,000,000**, rating **AAA / Aaa**, spread **3m SOFR + 1.45 %**.  \n  - *Class B*: **$60,000,000**, rating **AA / Aa2**, spread **3m SOFR + 2.10 %**.  \n  - *Class C*: **$32,500,000**, rating **A / A2**, spread **3m SOFR + 3.25 %**.  \n  - *Class D*: **$27,500,000**, rating **BBB / Baa2**, spread **3m SOFR + 4.50 %**.  \n  - *Class E*: **$20,000,000**, rating **BB / Ba2**, spread **3m SOFR + 7.85 %**.  \n- **Subordinated Notes** – **$70,000,000**, rating **NR**, residual terms.  \n\n**Notable Insights**\n\n- Senior notes total **$455,000,000** (91 % of target collateral); subordinated notes represent **$70,000,000** (14 % of target collateral).  \n- Spreads rise monotonically from Class A to Class E, reflecting increasing credit risk.  \n- The spread differential between the lowest‑rated senior note (Class E) and the highest‑rated senior note (Class A) is **6.40 percentage points** (7.85 % – 1.45 %).  \n- The legal maturity is 12 years from closing, with a 5‑year reinvestment period ending in 2031.  \n- Ratings span from **AAA / Aaa** for the most senior notes to **NR** for subordinated notes, illustrating a clear senior‑to‑junior hierarchy."
    }
